  "code": "2718",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"height: 76px; width: 81.7522%;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 11.5273%;\"><strong>&nbsp;Result</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 87.3805%;\"><strong>&nbsp;Remarls</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 11.5273%;\">&nbsp;Positive</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 87.3805%;\">&nbsp;Indicates presence of circulating Cryptococcus species complex Antigen</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 11.5273%;\">&nbsp;Negative</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 87.3805%;\">&nbsp;Indicates absence of circulating Cryptococcus species complex&nbsp; Antigen</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Positive results are seen in fungal disease of lungs, brain and meninges caused by Cryptococcus species complex (C. neoformans &amp; C. gattii). While the majority of C. neoformans infections occur in immunocompromised patients, C. gattii has a higher predilection for infection in healthy individuals.</li>\n<li>Negative results are seen in absence of Cryptococcus infection. However, it does not rule out the disease</li>\n<li>Results should be co-related with clinical condition and tests like microscopy and fungal culture.</li>\n<li>False positive results may be observed in patients with high levels of Rheumatoid factor, conditions like trichosporonosis, Capnocytophaga canimorus septicaemia, malignancy, &nbsp;Rothia &nbsp;bacteremia, &nbsp;usage &nbsp;of &nbsp;some &nbsp;soaps, &nbsp;disinfectants &nbsp;and hydroxyethyl starch (used for fluid resuscitation).</li>\n<li>False negative reaction may be due to processing of sample collected early in the course of disease or low threshold of antigen and due to prozone effect. The test should be repeated on a new specimen obtained after two weeks.</li>\n<li>Test conducted in CSF/serum.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br><strong>Uses</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>To diagnose disease caused by Cryptococcus species complex (C. neoformans &amp; C. gattii)<br><br></li>\n</ul>",
